    "description": "Storage Grip V2 (AR-15): FFFTech/FFFTechnology\n\nVersion 2 of the original 3FTech Storage Grip. Overall a longer and wider design. Overall grip width is 29.3mm, length is \nroughly 107mm. The V2 can hold 17 - 18 rounds of 9x19 NATO, versus the V1's capacity being only 10 - 11 rounds. \n\nThe storage hatch for V2 has been significantly strengthened compared to V1.\n\nHas two different textured locking tab hatches. \n\n\n\nPrinter Used: Ender 3 V2\n\nFilament Used: PLA+\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 220C \nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .20mm \nStandard Layer Height: .16mm\nWall Thickness: .40 \nWall Perimeters: 7+\nInfill: 25%\nInfill Pattern: Gyroid\nMaterial Flow: 100%\nSupport Material Percentage: 18% \n\n\n\nHardware Needed:\n\n1x Allen Head Screw, 1/4-28 x 1\"\n\n1x Steel Star Washer\n\n1x Safety Selector Detent Pin\n\n1x Safety Selector Detent Spring\n\n1x M3x12mm (or M3x15mm) Hex Set Screw\n\n\n\nNotes: \n\n1) Yes... I checked it's Skittle capacity; Storage Grip V2 can hold roughly a little over half a standard pack of Skittles. \n\n\n\nAccreditations:\n\ntheOtherSig: Printed and assembled the grip. Gave info that led to an improved lockup of the tabs to the inside of the grip, as \nwell as provided info for geometric edits to make hatch closure easier than previously designed. Provided video footage and images.\n\nEWW: Printed and assembled the grip. Provided footage and images. Provided info on 9x19 NATO capacity. (Somehow performed black magic \nfuckery and fit 19rds, max I could fit was 17.)",
